Package: pve-bindsnap
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: bitranox <rnowotny1966@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: perl, pve-container, libpve-guest-common-perl
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/bitranox/pve-bindsnap
Description: snapshot and clone Proxmox LXC containers with bind/device mounts
 Proxmox VE refuses snapshots and clones of LXC containers that carry bind or
 device mountpoints (mpN pointing at host paths). pve-bindsnap diverts
 PVE::LXC::Config and PVE::API2::LXC and loads a small overlay that hides those
 mountpoints from the snapshot code path and carries them to a clone, while
 delegating everything else to the live upstream code.
 .
 Both overrides are gated by content checksums of the upstream source: on a
 pve-container build that is not in the tested set, bind-mount snapshots need
 an explicit opt-in and clone stays stock. Removing the package restores the
 stock Proxmox modules.
